			<div class="content" id="post-content-2440098">
									

<p>Reading up about &quot;The Man at the Threshold&quot; was remarkably satisfying. Intended or otherwise, it's a really solid way to wrap this whole thing up.</p>
<p>The example logs in the middle did tend to draw on, and as a whole, didn't explore the concept as thoroughly as I thought you might. It all came off as a bit too sterilized, without some of the visceral ideas that the premise could support. To compare this to &quot;To End All Wars&quot;, that article is full of examples of the &quot;ends&quot; of an idea, while this one made me wonder why similar ideas weren't included (in terms of theme, not necessarily content). Not to say the examples used were bad ones, obviously. I still upvoted it.</p>
<p>The ending was good, though. The concept is brilliant, the setting is sublime, the image is top notch, and the title is perfect. Tower of Silence. I love it. Well done.</p>

